TurtleGit for Mac is an independent, unofficial port project.
Upstream TortoiseGit: https://github.com/TortoiseGit/TortoiseGit
Official upstream project: https://tortoisegit.org/
Upstream source and license are copyright their respective contributors.
The LICENSE file is retained from upstream TortoiseGit (GPL version 2).
No affiliation or endorsement by the upstream project is claimed.
New Swift implementation in this repository is licensed under GPL version 2.
The upstream audit baseline is documented in docs/upstream.json.
Apple frameworks and separately installed Git retain their own licenses.

Command and status icon artwork is copied unchanged from TortoiseGit resources.
Those icons were derived from the TortoiseSVN project: https://tortoisesvn.net/
The upstream notice also names https://tortoisesvn.tigris.org/ (historical site).
We use the GNU GPL alternative offered by the upstream resource license.
The original resource license, source paths and SHA-256 hashes are retained in
Sources/TurtleGitCore/Resources/Icons/ and bundled with the shared framework.
Copyright (c) 2006-2007 The TortoiseSVN Project. All rights reserved.

AppStore preparation bundles a pinned Git engine built from its unmodified
upstream source archive (https://www.kernel.org/pub/software/scm/git/). Git is
licensed under GPL v2. Its corresponding source archive, COPYING, retained
third-party notices and reconstruction scripts are included under
Contents/Helpers/Git/share/licenses/git/. Configuration/GitRuntime.json records
the version, source URL and checksum. macOS system libraries are not redistributed.

The app bundles EditorConfig C Core and statically linked PCRE2. Their original
license texts, pinned source/test archives and reconstruction script are retained
under Contents/Helpers/EditorConfig/. Configuration/EditorConfigRuntime.json
records source versions and checksums. EditorConfig includes Simplified/New/
Revised BSD and per-file notices; PCRE2 retains its BSD license and exceptions.
Consult the included license texts and complete corresponding sources.
